From 53e19c393e9a8dbd1e263e161fb4371a1599066f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "gastown.dog-2" <gastown.dog-2@gascity.local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:19:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ga-6u64fm): classify migrated result; migrate only into
 builder-readable rigs, one hop max

Gate ga-tguml6 failed the auto-migration on two blocking findings:

1. A successful migration read as a Pilot fault. DISPATCH_RESULT
   rig_native_dog_store_migrated was not classified in _pilot_sweep_emit, so
   every migration was tallied under failed_other, and the sweep-event
   selftest's own drift guard (B4) went red (50 passed / 1 failed vs 51/0 at
   the merge-base). It is now a refused_by_guard outcome keyed by name (the
   guard resolved the refusal), listed in KNOWN_RESULTS, the B4 explicit-name
   loop and an A2 case; the closure invariant still holds. It still returns 1
   and counts toward the Step 5 stall streak on purpose: that streak is what
   would notice a migration loop.

2. The destination could be another dog-store-blind rig, with no re-migration
   guard: gastown, lexbh and marketing map to gastown.dog in rig_to_builders,
   and the copy keeps the original text, so lexbh -> gastown -> lexbh ... hopped
   one new bead per 5-minute sweep. Now:
   - a candidate rig must pass the same predicate that made the source blind
     (_pilot_dog_store_blind_guard on the rig's own builder), so unknown rigs
     are never destinations and there is no second list to drift;
   - the text match is a tokenised path-component match (_pilot_text_names_rig_path):
     URLs, host.tld/... and word-suffixes no longer count; ~/ and absolute paths do;
   - _pilot_story_already_migrated: a story carrying gc.migrated_from (snapshot
     or live record, or unreadable metadata) is parked, never migrated twice.
   Also: warm the rig-list memo once (was two `gc rig list` per migration) and
   warn when the destination defaulted because rigs could not be listed.

Selftests: the reviewer's repros (a)(b)(c) both directions, anchoring, hop
guard, marker round-trip (writer key == reader key) and the cold-memo call
count are covered; each fix was mutation-tested (removing it fails exactly its
cases). bash 3.2 (/bin/bash) clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
